---
config:
    theme: base
    themeCSS: "text { font-family: Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif !important; }"
    themeVariables:
        background: "#0d1117"
        primaryColor: "#23213c"
        primaryTextColor: "#eeeeff"
        primaryBorderColor: "#7968fa"
        lineColor: "#a5a8ba"
        actorBkg: "#23213c"
        actorBorder: "#7968fa"
        actorTextColor: "#eeeeff"
        actorLineColor: "#727687"
        signalColor: "#b1b4c4"
        signalTextColor: "#e5e7eb"
        labelBoxBkgColor: "#151626"
        labelBoxBorderColor: "#7968fa"
        labelTextColor: "#eeeeff"
        loopTextColor: "#eeeeff"
        noteBkgColor: "#171c28"
        noteBorderColor: "#41506d"
        noteTextColor: "#c8d6ed"
        sequenceNumberColor: "#ffffff"
        fontFamily: "Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif"
    sequence:
        useMaxWidth: false
        width: 190
        actorMargin: 45
        messageMargin: 38
        wrap: true
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Application
    participant E as Microsoft Entra ID
    participant G as AI Gateway
    participant P as Policies<br/>(inside gateway)
    participant M as Foundry model
    participant O as Monitoring

    Note over C,O: Entra ID target flow - not yet configured for callers by this Terraform sample
    Note over C,G: With private-only ingress: application needs<br/>private DNS and a route to the gateway endpoint.<br/>An Entra token does not grant network access.
    C->>E: Acquire token for AI Gateway
    E-->>C: Caller access token
    C->>G: Prompt + alias<br/>Authorization: Bearer [caller token]
    G->>G: Validate token<br/>Check invocation role
    break Invalid token or insufficient access
        G-->>C: 401 / 403 - stop before inference
    end
    G->>P: Evaluate configured governance policies
    alt Allowed
        P-->>G: Allow
        opt No valid cached backend token
            G->>E: Use gateway<br/>managed identity
            E-->>G: Model-backend access token
        end
        G->>M: Forward using gateway identity token
        M->>M: Authorize gateway identity<br/>and run deployment
        M-->>G: Model response or backend error
        G-)O: Export tokens, latency and request telemetry
        G-->>C: Response
    else Blocked by policy
        P-->>G: Deny
        G-->>C: Policy error - no model invocation
        G-)O: Export policy rejection telemetry
    end
    Note over G,M: Caller token is not forwarded to the model.<br/>Backend access uses the gateway identity.
    Note over P,O: Telemetry export is asynchronous.<br/>Policies run inside AI Gateway.
